</document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8139503-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8139503</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1096597A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AOKI KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AOKI, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A balanced-to-unbalanced transforming circuit used in electric communication for feeding power from an unbalanced circuit serving as a power feeding line to a balanced line by means of a microstrip line.  Two microstrip center conductors are connected to a balanced line.  Signals whose phases are opposite to each other are inputted to the respective microstrip center conductors to transform the unbalanced current flowing through the microstrip line to a balanced current to flow through the balanced line.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un circuit permettant de transformer un courant non équilibré en courant équilibré, lequel circuit est utilisé en communication électrique pour fournir de l'énergie électrique provenant d'un circuit non équilibré servant de ligne d'alimentation électrique à une ligne équilibrée au moyen d'une ligne du type microbande. Deux conducteurs centraux du type microbande sont connectés à une ligne équilibrée. Les signaux dont les phases sont opposées sont introduits dans chacun des conducteurs centraux de type microbande de manière à transformer le courant non équilibré passant dans la ligne de type microbande en un courant équilibré passant dans la ligne équilibrée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>